    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and both its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner creation for this Spring Boot PetClinic REST app.\n\nThe challenge: the create flow validates the incoming `OwnerFieldsDto` via Bean Validation (generated from `openapi.yml`), which had `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'` on `telephone`. That would reject an input like `(04) 1234-5678` with a 400 *before* any normalization could run \u2014 failing the accept test. So the fix spans three coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` field: removed the digit-only `pattern` (kept `minLength: 1`/`maxLength: 20`) so raw, punctuated numbers reach the controller, and documented the normalization contract in the description.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After mapping the DTO, normalize the telephone via a new `normalizeTelephone` helper: strip every non-digit (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`), require exactly 10 digits, and store/return that value. Applied only on create, matching the spec (\"On create\").\n\n3. **New `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` + handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 Mirrors the existing `MissingOwnerFieldsException` pattern to reject a malformed telephone with a **400 Bad Request** (`errors: [\"telephone\"]`). A plain `ResponseStatusException` wouldn't have worked here because the advice's catch-all `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` maps everything to 500.\n\nThe `Owner` entity's existing `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")`/`@Digits` constraints are left intact \u2014 the normalized 10-digit value satisfies them, so they still guard the persisted invariant.\n\nBehavior now: `(04) 1234-5678` \u2192 stored/returned as `0412345678`; `12345` \u2192 400.",
